The volume of a [unit ball](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ball_(mathematics))
in $N$ dimensions (aka $N$-ball) is

$$f(N) = \frac{(2\pi)^{(N//2)}}{ (N!!) (2)^{ {(-1)}^N } } \tag{1}$$

where $N//2$ is
[integer division](https://mathworld.wolfram.com/IntegerDivision.html),
and $N!!$ is the
[double factorial](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Double_factorial).

For an $N$-ball with radius $R$,

$$Volume = R^N f(N) \tag{2}$$

$$Surface\ Area = \frac{d}{dR} Volume = N R^{(N-1)} f(N) \tag{3}$$

# Python code

```python
import math

# https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Double_factorial
def double_factorial(n):
  r = 1
  m = math.ceil(n/2) - 1
  for k in range(m):
    r *= (n - 2*k)
  return r

def unit_volume(N):
  return (2*math.pi)**(N//2) / double_factorial(N) / 2**(-1)**N

# volume of an N-ball
def volume(N, r=1.0):
  return unit_volume(N) * r**N

# surface area of an N-ball
def surface_area(N, r=1.0):
  return unit_volume(N) * N*r**(N-1)

# volume of a 2-ball (aka circle area)
def circle_area(r):
  return volume(2, r)

# surface area of a 2-ball (aka circle perimeter)
def circle_perimeter(r):
  return surface_area(2, r)

# volume of a 3-ball (aka sphere volume)
def sphere_volume(r):
  return volume(3, r)

# surface area of a 3-ball (aka sphere surface area)
def sphere_surface_area(r):
  return surface_area(3, r)



